1323:\begin{proof}
1324:%The proof is split into two parts. First we prove the statement about \MatchML and then the statement about \FactorML.
1325:
1326:We get the polynomial-time solvability of \MatchML for the case~$\ell\leq 2$ from \autoref{lemma:reductiontomaxweightmatching}. For the case of
1327:$\ell\geq 3$ we give a parameterized reduction from \MCC. %This reduction can
1328:%be adapted to the $c$-factor case.
1329: In \MCC, we are given an $h$-partite graph $H=(U_1\uplus \ldots\uplus U_h,F)$ and
1330:need to determine whether it contains a clique of size $h$.
1331:Note that such a clique necessarily contains exactly one vertex from each set
1332:$U_i$ and cliques of more than $h$ vertices are impossible. We say that
1333:vertices from $U_i$ have \emph{color}~$i$. 
1334: 
1335:\emph{Reduction idea.}\quad The main idea is to create the first two layers in such a way that selecting a subgraph that admits a perfect matching in both layers corresponds to selecting exactly one vertex of each color. The third layer is constructed in a way that each subgraph that admits perfect matchings in the first two layer admits also a perfect matching in this layer if all selected vertices are pairwise connected and hence form a multicolored clique.
1336: 
1337:
1338:Without loss of
1339:generality, we assume that the number~$h$ of colors is even.
1340: We construct an instance of \MatchML for $t=\ell=3$ as follows
1341: and then argue that the construction is easily generalizable to larger numbers of layers.
1342: 
1343: \emph{Vertices.}\quad
1344: % \proofparagraph{Vertices.}
1345: First, create $h-1$ vertices for each vertex in graph~$H$ (one vertex for each color other than its own color).
1346: Formally, for each color $1 \le j \le h$ and each~$u_i \in U_j$,
1347: create the vertex set $V_i$ consisting of the vertices~$v_{(i,j')}$, $j' \in
1348: (\{1,\dots,h\} \setminus \{j\})$.
1349: Second, create one \emph{color vertex} $w_j$ for each color~$j \in
1350: \{1,\dots,h\}$. We denote the set of color vertices as~$W:=\bigcup_{1 \le j \le
1351: h}\{w_j\}$.
1352:
1353:\emph{Vertex selection gadget by graphs~$G_1$
1354:and~$G_2$.}\quad The vertex selection gadget is intended to make sure the vertices selected in any valid solution of the constructed \MatchML instance correspond to pairwise differently colored vertices of~$H$.
1355:The vertex selection
1356: gadget is visualized in \autoref{fig:matching:selection}.
1357:We construct it as follows. For each color~$1 \le j \le h$, create for each~$u_i \in
1358:U_j$ one cycle on $\{w_j\} \cup V_i$ in the graph~$G_1 \cup G_2$
1359: such that the edges are alternatingly from $G_1$ and from $G_2$.
1360: These $|U_j|$~cycles are all of length~$h$ and share only the color vertex~$w_j$.
1361: To realize this, create the following edges.
1362: For each $1 \le z \le h-2$, create an edge in graph~$G_{(z\text{ mod }2)+1}$
1363: between $v_{(i,z)}$ and $v_{(i,z+1)}$ if $z<j-1$,
1364: between $v_{(i,z+1)}$ and $v_{(i,z+2)}$ if~$z\ge j$, and
1365: between $v_{(i,z)}$ and $v_{(i,z+2)}$ if $z=j-1$.
1366: Create an edge between $w_j$ and $v_{(i,1)}$ in graph~$G_2$,
1367: between $v_{(i,h)}$ and $w_j$ in graph~$G_1$ if $j\neq h$, and
1368: between $v_{(i,h-1)}$ and $w_j$ in graph~$G_1$ if $j= h$.
