1530: We show that $X:=W \cup V_1 \cup V_2 \cup \dots \cup V_h$ is
1531: a solution for our \MatchML instance.
1532: By construction, $X$~is of size $h+ h \cdot (h-1)=h^2 = k$.
1533: It remains to show that graph~$G_z[X]$ has a perfect matching for each $1 \le z \le 3$.
1534: Recall that we created for each color~$1 \le j \le h$ and for each vertex~$u_i
1535: \in U_j$ one cycle on $\{w_j\} \cup V_i$ in the graph~$G_1 \cup G_2$ such
1536: that the edges alternatingly are from $G_1$ and from $G_2$.
1537: Since $X$~only contains one of these cycles for each color,
1538: a perfect matching is easy to find for graph~$G_1[X]$ and for graph~$G_2[X]$.
1539: For graph~$G_3[X]$, we can find the matching~$\{ \{v_{(i,j)},v_{(j,i)}\} \mid (1 \le i,j \le h) \wedge (i \neq j)\} \cup \{
1540: \{w_j,w_{j+h/2}\} \mid 1 \le j \le h/2\}$, since, by construction, $v_{(i,j)}$ is
1541: adjacent to $v_{(j,i)}$ if $u_i$~is adjacent to
1542: $u_j$, and $u_i \in U_i$ and $u_j \in U_j$ (which is the case since~$K$ is a clique).
