codex
The bare pool held the original easy rung 0/3, but that rung cannot ship: the stronger 20-million-node exact attack solved 4/8 of its seeds. I’m therefore sliding the ladder upward—old medium becomes new easy, old hard becomes medium, and a larger rung becomes hard—then rerunning both local gates and the script-owned oracle evidence. This records the generic models’ failure without ignoring the specialist attack.
