The README and final report are written. I’ve explicitly documented the limits of the Track A claim: the paper proves worst-case hardness, the plant distribution is only empirically defended, the exact solver is custom rather than commercial, WL is not a complete canonical form, and one bare oracle response was length-limited. I’m doing a final interface/determinism/emit-compatibility audit now, without invoking `submit.sh` (which would commit and push).
