codex
The overtest identified a real scalability inefficiency—not a correctness failure: planting rebuilt the full adjacency structure after every 2-switch, making the largest rung unnecessarily slow. I stopped that redundant stress run and am replacing the rebuild with incremental neighbor updates. This preserves the exact RNG sequence and generated instances while reducing construction from repeated dense rescans to local switch updates. Per the gate rules, I’ll rerun the full self-test after the change.
apply patch
